498 0 obj
<<
/Title (The primary engine of the narrative relies on the dynamic interplay between internal character motivation and external hardship. Daniel faces a dual conflict: a character versus society/circumstance struggle against poverty, and a subtle character versus self conflict when fatigue tempts him to give up. The text notes that Daniel studied every evening while "the rain beat against the roof, and darkness covered the street," establishing an atmosphere of isolation and vulnerability. His family had little money, and "each day seemed to bring another problem". This harsh reality reaches a critical point when the electricity suddenly fails, pushing Daniel to a emotional crossroads where he briefly wants to close his books and sleep. However, his decision to reject passivity and actively search for an old candle demonstrates his profound internal strength. Rather than letting external limitations dictate his potential, Daniel takes active responsibility for his education. His actions reveal that true character is revealed not during moments of ease, but during moments of unexpected disruption.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 523 0 R
/Next 442 0 R
>>
endobj
